                    insight_award:          `Award-worthy: a rigorous diagnosis, a transfer-led design inside the £1.8M cap, level 3–4 measurement on an attributable metric, and an honest, attribution-backed ROI. You secured the £360,000 and the kind of proof that wins EFMD-shortlisted work — and renews a 22%-of-turnover account.`,
                    insight_feekept:        `You secured the £360,000 at-risk fee by staking it on an attributable metric with a credible isolation method — but the wider case has soft spots. The contingent money is safe; the renewal still depends on tightening diagnosis, transfer or impact.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `Your design exceeded the £1.8M ceiling, so it could not be contracted as proposed — and the at-risk fee went with it. A superb programme Brackenmoor cannot buy loses to a rival's good-enough one that fits.`,
                    insight_feelost:        `The £360,000 is at risk: you staked it on a metric you can't attribute, measured too low, or both. Even if the leaders genuinely improved, you've designed a fee you can lose to confounders — and a board that won't renew.`,
                    insight_misdiagnosed:   `Diagnostic rigour stayed low: you treated the CEO's presenting symptom instead of the structural root the data revealed. Everything built on a wrong diagnosis inherits the error.`,
                    insight_notransfer:     `Transfer strength is weak — the design loaded contact hours or scaled cheaply without the manager reinforcement, application and accountability that turn learning into behaviour. Most of it will evaporate within weeks.`,
